cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RetryTaxBench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "RetryTaxBench"
abstract: >-
  A PostgreSQL benchmarking harness that adds a configurable cap on the
  number of times an aborted transaction may be retried (the retry budget)
  to the SmallBank workload, and measures how that cap changes the
  throughput/reliability trade-off across Read Committed, Snapshot
  Isolation, Serializable Snapshot Isolation, and mixed isolation-level
  allocations.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Oliver
    affiliation: "University of Sydney"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZhangO999/retry-tax-bench"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - databases
  - transaction-processing
  - isolation-levels
  - postgresql
  - smallbank
  - benchmarking
